{"title":"Zero module","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>zero module</b> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Module\" title=\"Module\">module</a> with one element, whose group structure\nis that of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Trivial_group\" title=\"Trivial group\">trivial group</a>, and whose <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ring\" title=\"Ring\">ring</a> acts trivially upon it.\nTechnically speaking, for any ring <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> there are infinitely many left zero\nmodules, but they are trivially <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Isomorphic\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Isomorphic\">isomorphic</a>, so by abuse of language\nwe often refer to <i>the</i> zero module.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ring\" title=\"Ring\">ring</a>, then every zero module is an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Initial_object&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Initial object (page does not exist)\">initial object</a>\nand a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Terminal_object&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Terminal object (page does not exist)\">terminal object</a> in the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Category\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Category\">category</a> of left <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />-modules.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Zero_module&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Zero_module&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Trivial_group\" title=\"Trivial group\">Trivial group</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Zero_ring\" title=\"Zero ring\">Zero ring</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018114458\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.019 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 34/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 274/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 513/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.402      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.402      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8347:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018114458 and revision id 32659. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}